From: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
Date: Mon, 26 May 2025 16:56:46 +0800
Subject: crypto: shash - Fix buffer overrun in import function
Patch-mainline: v6.16-rc1
Git-commit: 0a84874c7e7dde5cdddc80a82093120e924a348b
References: jsc#PED-15972

Only set the partial block length to zero if the algorithm is
block-only.  Otherwise the descriptor context could be empty,
e.g., for digest_null.

Reported-by: syzbot+4851c19615d35f0e4d68@syzkaller.appspotmail.com
Fixes: 7650f826f7b2 ("crypto: shash - Handle partial blocks in API")
Signed-off-by: Herbert Xu <herbert@gondor.apana.org.au>
[nstange@suse.de: apply to crypto_shash_import_core() instead of to
 __crypto_shash_import(), introduced only with (skipped)
 c6a12f394c48 ("crypto: hash - Add export_core and import_core hooks").]
Acked-by: Nicolai Stange <nstange@suse.de>
---
 crypto/shash.c |    9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/crypto/shash.c
+++ b/crypto/shash.c
@@ -250,12 +250,13 @@ int crypto_shash_import_core(struct shas
 	if (crypto_shash_get_flags(tfm) & CRYPTO_TFM_NEED_KEY)
 		return -ENOKEY;
 
-	plen = crypto_shash_blocksize(tfm) + 1;
-	descsize = crypto_shash_descsize(tfm);
 	ss = crypto_shash_statesize(tfm);
-	buf[descsize - 1] = 0;
-	if (crypto_shash_block_only(tfm))
+	if (crypto_shash_block_only(tfm)) {
+		plen = crypto_shash_blocksize(tfm) + 1;
 		ss -= plen;
+		descsize = crypto_shash_descsize(tfm);
+		buf[descsize - 1] = 0;
+	}
 	import = crypto_shash_alg(tfm)->import;
 	if (!import) {
 		memcpy(buf, in, ss);
